{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CellDepthTruncation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CellDepthTruncation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.witness_hyp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.witness_hyp","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L155-L161","doc":"The hypotheses are satisfiable: `q = 2`, `z = 1` over `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.no_stable_phi_tower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.no_stable_phi_tower","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**The conjunction in the original claim is inconsistent.** No sequence can both\n(i) equal `Φ_q^{[≤K]}(z)` at every truncation level `K` and (ii) be constant from some\nlevel `k⋆` on, when `q ≠ 0`, `z ≠ 0` and no pole is hit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_succ_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_succ_ne","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L126-L143","doc":"**The `Φ_q` side does not stabilise.** For `q ≠ 0`, `z ≠ 0` and no pole hit,\n`Φ_q^{[≤K+1]}(z) ≠ Φ_q^{[≤K]}(z)` for every `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L121-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc_succ","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L117-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.phiTrunc","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L114-L115","doc":"`Φ_q^{[≤K]}(z) = ∏_{j=1}^{K} (1 - q^{-j} z)^{-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.kstar_eq_of_max_in_supp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.kstar_eq_of_max_in_supp","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L100-L106","doc":"**Vacuity.** If some block of maximal depth lies in the support, `k⋆` is the global\nmaximum, so the truncation removes nothing. For `H_n(q)` and `x = T_w` (or any braid\nimage) this applies: the index and sign characters `q^{ℓ(w)}`, `(-q⁻¹)^{ℓ(w)}` never\nvanish, and both the `a`-function and `gbDepth` attain their maximum on one of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.tower_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.tower_total","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L71-L98","doc":"**Reconstruction.** With unit weights the truncated tower is the whole trace\n`τ(x) = Σ_λ τ(e_λ x)` (since `Σ_λ e_λ = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.tower_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.tower_stable","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L57-L69","doc":"**Stabilisation.** For arbitrary weights `α_k`, the weighted tower truncated at any\n`K ≥ k⋆` equals the tower truncated at `k⋆`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:cell-depth-truncation","label":"prop:cell-depth-truncation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.stratum_eq_zero_of_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.stratum_eq_zero_of_gt","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L47-L55","doc":"**Vanishing lemma.** Every stratum strictly above `k⋆` is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.le_kstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.le_kstar","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L44-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.stratum","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The depth-`k` stratum `m^(k)(x) = τ(E_k x) = Σ_{d λ = k} τ(e_λ x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.kstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.kstar","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L37-L38","doc":"`k⋆(x)`: the maximal depth over the support (`0` if the support is empty). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.supp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellDepthTruncation.supp","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cell-depth-truncation.lean#L34-L35","doc":"Support of the block-coefficient vector: the blocks where `τ(e_λ x) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}